#
# prima-materia — chaos magic: Carroll, Chaoism and Chaos Magic
#
# The harvest of one work of the corpus of pmt:ChaosMagic, kept apart from
# traditions/chaos-magic.ttl, which declares the tradition and the work
# (pmw:ChaoismAndChaosMagic) and carries its reading note and harvest counts.
# Harvested complete under prima-materia#893 with two independent extraction
# passes over the whole essay, in the order of the text. Cited by leaf of the
# four-leaf PDF read, which carries no page numbers; the printing in Chaos
# International no. 10, pp. 11-13, was not opened. Conditions of failure carry
# a note beginning "Counted as a condition of failure:".
#

pmc:ChaosMagicChaoPersonal a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Chaoism as one practitioner's view, not a doctrine of the current"@en, "Chaoismus als Sicht eines Praktikers, nicht als Lehre der Strömung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author speaks only for his own Chaoism and Chaos Magic, since there are as many versions of it as there are Chaoists who practise magic; no common doctrine is claimed for the current."@en ;
    skos:note "A statement on how fixed the system is: it has no shared body of doctrine."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ChaoismAndChaosMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Chaoism and Chaos Magic: A Personal View (electronic copy without imprint, a PDF of four leaves made on 2003-07-31 from a word-processor file; printed earlier in Chaos International no. 10, pp. 11-13, by a collection of excerpts dated 1993), leaf 1 of 4; read in the born-digital text layer of that PDF in the open scan archive item peter-j.-carroll-chaoism-and-chaos-magic" .

pmc:ChaosMagicChaoMetaBelief a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The one-line definition: belief is an instrument for effects and not an end"@en, "Die Definition in einer Zeile: Glaube ist ein Werkzeug für Wirkungen und kein Selbstzweck"@de ;
    skos:definition "Offered as a definition most Chaoists would probably not dispute: Chaoists usually hold the higher-order belief that a belief is a means of producing effects and not a goal in itself."@en ;
    skos:note "The same claim stands in Liber Kaos (pmc:ChaosMagicBeliefAsTool); here it is given as the definition of the current, hedged as what most Chaoists would probably accept."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ChaoismAndChaosMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Chaoism and Chaos Magic: A Personal View (electronic copy without imprint, a PDF of four leaves made on 2003-07-31 from a word-processor file; printed earlier in Chaos International no. 10, pp. 11-13, by a collection of excerpts dated 1993), leaf 1 of 4; read in the born-digital text layer of that PDF in the open scan archive item peter-j.-carroll-chaoism-and-chaos-magic" .

pmc:ChaosMagicChaoChangingOwnBeliefs a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The ability to alter the beliefs one is subject to"@en, "Die Fähigkeit, die Überzeugungen zu ändern, denen man unterliegt"@de ;
    skos:definition "People are said to be able to modify the beliefs of which they are victims, should they wish to; the essay names the ability in passing and gives no method for it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ChaoismAndChaosMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Chaoism and Chaos Magic: A Personal View (electronic copy without imprint, a PDF of four leaves made on 2003-07-31 from a word-processor file; printed earlier in Chaos International no. 10, pp. 11-13, by a collection of excerpts dated 1993), leaf 1 of 4; read in the born-digital text layer of that PDF in the open scan archive item peter-j.-carroll-chaoism-and-chaos-magic" .

pmc:ChaosMagicChaoOwnBeliefsCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "One rarely sees how far one is the victim of one's own beliefs"@en, "Man sieht selten, wie weit man Opfer der eigenen Überzeugungen ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Other people and cultures are easily seen as victims of their beliefs, but we seldom stop to ask how far we are victims of ours; the warning opens the essay's case against the belief in material causality."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicChaoChangingOwnBeliefs ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ChaoismAndChaosMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Chaoism and Chaos Magic: A Personal View (electronic copy without imprint, a PDF of four leaves made on 2003-07-31 from a word-processor file; printed earlier in Chaos International no. 10, pp. 11-13, by a collection of excerpts dated 1993), leaf 1 of 4; read in the born-digital text layer of that PDF in the open scan archive item peter-j.-carroll-chaoism-and-chaos-magic" .

pmc:ChaosMagicChaoMaterialCausalityObsession a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Material causality as the collective obsession of the present"@en, "Die materielle Kausalität als kollektive Obsession der Gegenwart"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author asserts that the dominant belief of every Western culture is that the universe works by material causes and so lies open to reason; grown since the Enlightenment, it is held to be stronger than the medieval belief in God and to look as limiting to future historians, and most people cannot imagine not holding it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ChaoismAndChaosMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Chaoism and Chaos Magic: A Personal View (electronic copy without imprint, a PDF of four leaves made on 2003-07-31 from a word-processor file; printed earlier in Chaos International no. 10, pp. 11-13, by a collection of excerpts dated 1993), leaves 1-2 of 4; read in the born-digital text layer of that PDF in the open scan archive item peter-j.-carroll-chaoism-and-chaos-magic" .

pmc:ChaosMagicChaoFreeWillContradiction a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Free will as a second belief that contradicts the first"@en, "Der freie Wille als zweiter Glaube, der dem ersten widerspricht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Nearly everyone is said to hold, beside material causality, a belief in something called free will which contradicts it and which they cannot specify."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ChaoismAndChaosMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Chaoism and Chaos Magic: A Personal View (electronic copy without imprint, a PDF of four leaves made on 2003-07-31 from a word-processor file; printed earlier in Chaos International no. 10, pp. 11-13, by a collection of excerpts dated 1993), leaf 2 of 4; read in the born-digital text layer of that PDF in the open scan archive item peter-j.-carroll-chaoism-and-chaos-magic" .

pmc:ChaosMagicChaoIconoclasticQuest a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The magician's function of breaking through beyond the normal, aimed at a culture's primary beliefs"@en, "Die Aufgabe des Magiers, über das Normale hinauszubrechen, gerichtet gegen die Grundüberzeugungen einer Kultur"@de ;
    skos:definition "Part of the magician's task is to push past ordinary reality. The author's quest has been antinomian and iconoclastic, and he chose to attack the primary beliefs of his culture: first material causality, second most of what passes for modern psychology."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ChaoismAndChaosMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Chaoism and Chaos Magic: A Personal View (electronic copy without imprint, a PDF of four leaves made on 2003-07-31 from a word-processor file; printed earlier in Chaos International no. 10, pp. 11-13, by a collection of excerpts dated 1993), leaf 2 of 4; read in the born-digital text layer of that PDF in the open scan archive item peter-j.-carroll-chaoism-and-chaos-magic" .

pmc:ChaosMagicChaoSatanismCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Attacking religion squanders iconoclastic effort"@en, "Der Angriff auf die Religion vergeudet ikonoklastische Kraft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Religion is held to have been fatally disabled already by the Renaissance sorcerers and scientists, so that Satanism, as a gesture against religion, wastes iconoclastic talent and contemporary Satanists waste their effort."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicChaoIconoclasticQuest ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ChaoismAndChaosMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Chaoism and Chaos Magic: A Personal View (electronic copy without imprint, a PDF of four leaves made on 2003-07-31 from a word-processor file; printed earlier in Chaos International no. 10, pp. 11-13, by a collection of excerpts dated 1993), leaves 1-2 of 4; read in the born-digital text layer of that PDF in the open scan archive item peter-j.-carroll-chaoism-and-chaos-magic" .

pmc:ChaosMagicChaoAgainstMagicalEnergy a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magical energy and magical force rejected as metaphors borrowed from material causality"@en, "Magische Energie und magische Kraft als Metaphern aus der materiellen Kausalität verworfen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Since spiritual accounts of magic fell away, causal-materialist belief has been used carelessly to coin metaphors of magical energy or force, tacitly taken to resemble static electricity or radio waves. The author calls this nonsense: magic can sometimes be made to behave a little like it, but it is a poor description."@en ;
    skos:note "A statement on the model, not on a practice; the essay gives no test that would tell the two descriptions apart."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ChaoismAndChaosMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Chaoism and Chaos Magic: A Personal View (electronic copy without imprint, a PDF of four leaves made on 2003-07-31 from a word-processor file; printed earlier in Chaos International no. 10, pp. 11-13, by a collection of excerpts dated 1993), leaf 2 of 4; read in the born-digital text layer of that PDF in the open scan archive item peter-j.-carroll-chaoism-and-chaos-magic" .

pmc:ChaosMagicChaoNonMaterialCausality a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Non-material causality working by probability"@en, "Nichtmaterielle Kausalität, die nach Wahrscheinlichkeit wirkt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reading Bohr's Copenhagen Interpretation, the author holds that reality is better modelled as non-material causality working probabilistically rather than deterministically, which ends the clockwork paradigm of the last two centuries."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ChaoismAndChaosMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Chaoism and Chaos Magic: A Personal View (electronic copy without imprint, a PDF of four leaves made on 2003-07-31 from a word-processor file; printed earlier in Chaos International no. 10, pp. 11-13, by a collection of excerpts dated 1993), leaf 2 of 4; read in the born-digital text layer of that PDF in the open scan archive item peter-j.-carroll-chaoism-and-chaos-magic" .

pmc:ChaosMagicChaoEinsteinDispute a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Einstein's opposition to quantum physics held to be a matter of faith"@en, "Einsteins Widerstand gegen die Quantenphysik als Glaubenssache gedeutet"@de ;
    skos:definition "Most orthodox scientists are said to dislike quantum physics the way a cleric dislikes witchcraft and to avoid its implications; Einstein, repelled by them out of faith in science and a remnant of Jewish belief, is said to have spent much of his later life fighting it without result."@en ;
    skos:note "Entered as a conceptualizing node: only the author's side is read, so it is not a dispute in the sense of the graph."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ChaoismAndChaosMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Chaoism and Chaos Magic: A Personal View (electronic copy without imprint, a PDF of four leaves made on 2003-07-31 from a word-processor file; printed earlier in Chaos International no. 10, pp. 11-13, by a collection of excerpts dated 1993), leaves 2-3 of 4; read in the born-digital text layer of that PDF in the open scan archive item peter-j.-carroll-chaoism-and-chaos-magic" .

pmc:ChaosMagicChaoMagicCentral a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magic as central to how the universe works"@en, "Magie als zentral für das Wirken des Universums"@de ;
    skos:definition "Quantum physics is read by the author as saying that magic is possible in a world more chaotic than thought and lies at the heart of how the universe works, which is magical and not a clockwork; he believes quantum physics to be at bottom a study of the magic that lies beneath what has been perceived as non-magical reality for two hundred years."@en ;
    skos:note "The text layer drops a word in the first clause; an excerpt collection of 1993 marks the same gap."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ChaoismAndChaosMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Chaoism and Chaos Magic: A Personal View (electronic copy without imprint, a PDF of four leaves made on 2003-07-31 from a word-processor file; printed earlier in Chaos International no. 10, pp. 11-13, by a collection of excerpts dated 1993), leaf 3 of 4; read in the born-digital text layer of that PDF in the open scan archive item peter-j.-carroll-chaoism-and-chaos-magic" .

pmc:ChaosMagicChaoCausalismAsPrison a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Causal materialism, once a liberation, now a prison that rules out magic"@en, "Der kausale Materialismus, einst Befreiung, jetzt ein Gefängnis, das Magie ausschließt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Causal materialist beliefs freed people from fifteen centuries of monotheism but have become tyranny at their zenith; relativity and its physics, as a near-final refinement of that paradigm, would confine us to this planet for ever and exclude magic, and quantum physics shows the way out."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ChaoismAndChaosMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Chaoism and Chaos Magic: A Personal View (electronic copy without imprint, a PDF of four leaves made on 2003-07-31 from a word-processor file; printed earlier in Chaos International no. 10, pp. 11-13, by a collection of excerpts dated 1993), leaf 3 of 4; read in the born-digital text layer of that PDF in the open scan archive item peter-j.-carroll-chaoism-and-chaos-magic" .

pmc:ChaosMagicChaoParadigmForecast a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Forecast: humanity will come to believe the magical paradigm in its guts"@en, "Vorhersage: die Menschheit wird das magische Paradigma verinnerlichen"@de ;
    skos:definition "It may take time, but eventually a significant part of humanity is predicted to believe the new paradigm at gut level and live by it; until then it will sound like confusion or dressed-up intellectualism to most."@en ;
    skos:note "A prediction about the world without a date; nothing in the essay says what would count against it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ChaoismAndChaosMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Chaoism and Chaos Magic: A Personal View (electronic copy without imprint, a PDF of four leaves made on 2003-07-31 from a word-processor file; printed earlier in Chaos International no. 10, pp. 11-13, by a collection of excerpts dated 1993), leaf 3 of 4; read in the born-digital text layer of that PDF in the open scan archive item peter-j.-carroll-chaoism-and-chaos-magic" .

pmc:ChaosMagicChaoColonialSelf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Humans as colonial beings of many personalities, without free will"@en, "Menschen als koloniale Wesen aus vielen Persönlichkeiten, ohne freien Willen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author rejects the post-monotheistic Western view of the person as a single unitary being with free will. He prefers to describe us as colonial beings made of multiple personalities, mostly spared the selective amnesia that marks that condition elsewhere, and holds that there is no free will."@en ;
    skos:note "Mentioned in passing and, by the author's own words, without explanation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ChaoismAndChaosMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Chaoism and Chaos Magic: A Personal View (electronic copy without imprint, a PDF of four leaves made on 2003-07-31 from a word-processor file; printed earlier in Chaos International no. 10, pp. 11-13, by a collection of excerpts dated 1993), leaf 3 of 4; read in the born-digital text layer of that PDF in the open scan archive item peter-j.-carroll-chaoism-and-chaos-magic" .

pmc:ChaosMagicChaoStochasticAction a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The capacity to act at random and to identify with the result"@en, "Die Fähigkeit, zufällig zu handeln und sich mit dem Ergebnis zu identifizieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "In place of free will, humans are said to have the ability to act at random, more precisely stochastically, and the tendency to identify with whatever they then find themselves doing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ChaoismAndChaosMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Chaoism and Chaos Magic: A Personal View (electronic copy without imprint, a PDF of four leaves made on 2003-07-31 from a word-processor file; printed earlier in Chaos International no. 10, pp. 11-13, by a collection of excerpts dated 1993), leaf 3 of 4; read in the born-digital text layer of that PDF in the open scan archive item peter-j.-carroll-chaoism-and-chaos-magic" .

pmc:ChaosMagicChaoGodsNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Gods and goddesses, held to be within us and about us as non-local information"@en, "Götter und Göttinnen, als in uns und um uns seiende nichtlokale Information gehalten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Every god and goddess is held to dwell inside us and also, without matter, around us as information that is not bound to a place."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "gods and goddesses" ;
    pm:nameRole "presences within the person and, non-materially, about it as non-local information" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ChaoismAndChaosMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Chaoism and Chaos Magic: A Personal View (electronic copy without imprint, a PDF of four leaves made on 2003-07-31 from a word-processor file; printed earlier in Chaos International no. 10, pp. 11-13, by a collection of excerpts dated 1993), leaf 3 of 4; read in the born-digital text layer of that PDF in the open scan archive item peter-j.-carroll-chaoism-and-chaos-magic" .

pmc:ChaosMagicChaoAllByMagic a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "All events happen by magic; causality is the statistically dependable pole of a range"@en, "Alles geschieht durch Magie; Kausalität ist das statistisch verlässliche Ende eines Spektrums"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author considers that all events basically occur by magic; the apparent causality studied by classical science is only the more statistically dependable pole of a range that runs out, at its opposite pole, into total Chaos."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ChaoismAndChaosMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Chaoism and Chaos Magic: A Personal View (electronic copy without imprint, a PDF of four leaves made on 2003-07-31 from a word-processor file; printed earlier in Chaos International no. 10, pp. 11-13, by a collection of excerpts dated 1993), leaf 3 of 4; read in the born-digital text layer of that PDF in the open scan archive item peter-j.-carroll-chaoism-and-chaos-magic" .

pmc:ChaosMagicChaoTwoAspects a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The two aspects of magic: parapsychological and psychological"@en, "Die zwei Seiten der Magie: parapsychologisch und psychologisch"@de ;
    skos:definition "For the author magic has two main aspects. The parapsychological one is enchantment and divination, in which the magician deals with nature by non-material causality; the psychological one, as the following paragraph treats it, is the dealing with apparently sentient sources traditionally named spirits, deities, demons and elementals."@en ;
    skos:note "The essay names the two aspects in one sentence and assigns only the first explicitly; the assignment of the second follows the order of the paragraphs. An ordering by the author, entered as conceptualizing because the essay carries no date on which it was made; the printing in Chaos International is earlier than December 1993."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ChaoismAndChaosMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Chaoism and Chaos Magic: A Personal View (electronic copy without imprint, a PDF of four leaves made on 2003-07-31 from a word-processor file; printed earlier in Chaos International no. 10, pp. 11-13, by a collection of excerpts dated 1993), leaves 3-4 of 4; read in the born-digital text layer of that PDF in the open scan archive item peter-j.-carroll-chaoism-and-chaos-magic" .

pmc:ChaosMagicChaoInformationExchange a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Enchantment and divination as an exchange of information with the environment"@en, "Verzauberung und Divination als Informationsaustausch mit der Umgebung"@de ;
    skos:definition "In enchantment and divination the author believes the magician tries to interact with nature through non-material causality, exchanging information with the environment without the use of bodily faculties."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ChaoismAndChaosMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Chaoism and Chaos Magic: A Personal View (electronic copy without imprint, a PDF of four leaves made on 2003-07-31 from a word-processor file; printed earlier in Chaos International no. 10, pp. 11-13, by a collection of excerpts dated 1993), leaf 3 of 4; read in the born-digital text layer of that PDF in the open scan archive item peter-j.-carroll-chaoism-and-chaos-magic" .

pmc:ChaosMagicChaoEnchantment a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Enchantment: acting on the environment by non-material causality"@en, "Verzauberung: Einwirken auf die Umgebung durch nichtmaterielle Kausalität"@de ;
    skos:definition "The capacity to affect nature by passing information to it through non-material causality, without physical means."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ChaoismAndChaosMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Chaoism and Chaos Magic: A Personal View (electronic copy without imprint, a PDF of four leaves made on 2003-07-31 from a word-processor file; printed earlier in Chaos International no. 10, pp. 11-13, by a collection of excerpts dated 1993), leaf 3 of 4; read in the born-digital text layer of that PDF in the open scan archive item peter-j.-carroll-chaoism-and-chaos-magic" .

pmc:ChaosMagicChaoDivination a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Divination: taking information from the environment without the physical faculties"@en, "Divination: Information aus der Umgebung ohne die physischen Fähigkeiten aufnehmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The capacity to receive information from the environment through non-material causality, without using the physical faculties."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ChaoismAndChaosMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Chaoism and Chaos Magic: A Personal View (electronic copy without imprint, a PDF of four leaves made on 2003-07-31 from a word-processor file; printed earlier in Chaos International no. 10, pp. 11-13, by a collection of excerpts dated 1993), leaf 3 of 4; read in the born-digital text layer of that PDF in the open scan archive item peter-j.-carroll-chaoism-and-chaos-magic" .

pmp:ChaosMagicChaoSpareManoeuvres a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Spare's mental manoeuvres, clothed in any form chosen at random"@en, "Spares geistige Manöver, in eine beliebig gewählte Form gekleidet"@de ;
    skos:definition "Austin Osman Spare is said to have identified exactly the mental manoeuvres that let the non-material exchange of enchantment and divination occur. They are called startlingly simple; the manoeuvre is to be kept, and its expression may be anything, picked at random."@en ;
    skos:note "The essay names the manoeuvres and does not describe them; the practice is entered with the one rule it states, fixed manoeuvre and free form."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ChaoismAndChaosMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Chaoism and Chaos Magic: A Personal View (electronic copy without imprint, a PDF of four leaves made on 2003-07-31 from a word-processor file; printed earlier in Chaos International no. 10, pp. 11-13, by a collection of excerpts dated 1993), leaves 3-4 of 4; read in the born-digital text layer of that PDF in the open scan archive item peter-j.-carroll-chaoism-and-chaos-magic" .

pmc:ChaosMagicChaoSpareYieldsEnchantment a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Spare's manoeuvres allow enchantment to occur"@en, "Spares Manöver lassen Verzauberung geschehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The mental manoeuvres Spare identified are said to be what is needed for the non-material action on nature in enchantment to take place."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicChaoSpareManoeuvres ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicChaoEnchantment ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ChaoismAndChaosMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Chaoism and Chaos Magic: A Personal View (electronic copy without imprint, a PDF of four leaves made on 2003-07-31 from a word-processor file; printed earlier in Chaos International no. 10, pp. 11-13, by a collection of excerpts dated 1993), leaf 3 of 4; read in the born-digital text layer of that PDF in the open scan archive item peter-j.-carroll-chaoism-and-chaos-magic" .

pmc:ChaosMagicChaoSpareYieldsDivination a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Spare's manoeuvres allow divination to occur"@en, "Spares Manöver lassen Divination geschehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The mental manoeuvres Spare identified are said to be what is needed for the non-material reception of information in divination to take place."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicChaoSpareManoeuvres ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicChaoDivination ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ChaoismAndChaosMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Chaoism and Chaos Magic: A Personal View (electronic copy without imprint, a PDF of four leaves made on 2003-07-31 from a word-processor file; printed earlier in Chaos International no. 10, pp. 11-13, by a collection of excerpts dated 1993), leaf 3 of 4; read in the born-digital text layer of that PDF in the open scan archive item peter-j.-carroll-chaoism-and-chaos-magic" .

pmc:ChaosMagicChaoUnlimitedSpells a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The capacity to devise spells and divinations without limit"@en, "Die Fähigkeit, beliebig viele Zauber und Formen der Divination zu entwerfen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Whoever has understood Spare's manoeuvres is said to be able to devise spells and ways of divining without limit."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ChaoismAndChaosMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Chaoism and Chaos Magic: A Personal View (electronic copy without imprint, a PDF of four leaves made on 2003-07-31 from a word-processor file; printed earlier in Chaos International no. 10, pp. 11-13, by a collection of excerpts dated 1993), leaves 3-4 of 4; read in the born-digital text layer of that PDF in the open scan archive item peter-j.-carroll-chaoism-and-chaos-magic" .

pmc:ChaosMagicChaoManoeuvresBeforeSpells a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Understanding the manoeuvres comes before inventing spells"@en, "Das Verständnis der Manöver geht dem Erfinden von Zaubern voraus"@de ;
    skos:definition "The unlimited invention of spells and divinations is said to follow once the manoeuvres have been understood."@en ;
    skos:note "The sentence gives the order and no consequence of skipping it; entered at prescribed order."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicChaoSpareManoeuvres ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicChaoUnlimitedSpells ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ChaoismAndChaosMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Chaoism and Chaos Magic: A Personal View (electronic copy without imprint, a PDF of four leaves made on 2003-07-31 from a word-processor file; printed earlier in Chaos International no. 10, pp. 11-13, by a collection of excerpts dated 1993), leaves 3-4 of 4; read in the born-digital text layer of that PDF in the open scan archive item peter-j.-carroll-chaoism-and-chaos-magic" .

pmc:ChaosMagicChaoSacredManoeuvres a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The manoeuvres are sacred, the forms of their expression arbitrary"@en, "Die Manöver sind heilig, die Formen ihres Ausdrucks beliebig"@de ;
    skos:definition "The inner manoeuvres are held sacred and fixed, while the forms in which they are expressed are arbitrary and can be anything taken at random."@en ;
    skos:note "A statement on how fixed the method is: what is fixed is the manoeuvre, never the symbol."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ChaoismAndChaosMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Chaoism and Chaos Magic: A Personal View (electronic copy without imprint, a PDF of four leaves made on 2003-07-31 from a word-processor file; printed earlier in Chaos International no. 10, pp. 11-13, by a collection of excerpts dated 1993), leaf 4 of 4; read in the born-digital text layer of that PDF in the open scan archive item peter-j.-carroll-chaoism-and-chaos-magic" .

pmc:ChaosMagicChaoBohrNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Bohr, a saint of the Church of Chaos"@en, "Bohr, ein Heiliger der Kirche des Chaos"@de ;
    skos:definition "The physicist Niels Bohr is counted by the author among the holy figures of his Church of Chaos, for the Copenhagen Interpretation."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Bohr" ;
    pm:nameRole "saint of the Church of Chaos" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ChaoismAndChaosMagic ;
