pmc:ChaosMagicChaoSpiritsNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Spirits, gods, demons and elementals, held to be resources within each person"@en, "Geister, Götter, Dämonen und Elementare, als Ressourcen in jedem Menschen gehalten"@de ;
    skos:definition "What seem to be conscious sources of knowing, inspiration and paranormal power, traditionally named spirits, gods, demons and elementals, are held to be remarkable resources present in every person; once roused they may also take in something from outside through non-material causality."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "spirits, gods, demons and elementals" ;
    pm:nameRole "seemingly conscious sources of knowing, inspiration and paranormal power within the person" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ChaoismAndChaosMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Chaoism and Chaos Magic: A Personal View (electronic copy without imprint, a PDF of four leaves made on 2003-07-31 from a word-processor file; printed earlier in Chaos International no. 10, pp. 11-13, by a collection of excerpts dated 1993), leaf 4 of 4; read in the born-digital text layer of that PDF in the open scan archive item peter-j.-carroll-chaoism-and-chaos-magic" .

pmc:ChaosMagicChaoInnerMultitude a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "An inner multitude and the collective unconscious make the possibilities almost limitless"@en, "Eine innere Vielheit und das kollektive Unbewusste machen die Möglichkeiten nahezu grenzenlos"@de ;
    skos:definition "Because everyone contains a rich multitude in the unconscious or subconscious and may in addition draw matching material from the collective unconscious, the possibilities are said to be practically limitless."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ChaoismAndChaosMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Chaoism and Chaos Magic: A Personal View (electronic copy without imprint, a PDF of four leaves made on 2003-07-31 from a word-processor file; printed earlier in Chaos International no. 10, pp. 11-13, by a collection of excerpts dated 1993), leaf 4 of 4; read in the born-digital text layer of that PDF in the open scan archive item peter-j.-carroll-chaoism-and-chaos-magic" .

pmc:ChaosMagicChaoInvokeAnything a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "With the right method any being can be invoked or evoked, even one newly thought of"@en, "Mit der richtigen Technik lässt sich alles invozieren oder evozieren, auch was vorher nicht bestand"@de ;
    skos:definition "With the right method, a magician is said to be capable of invoking or evoking any being, even beings that had no existence until the idea of summoning them arose."@en ;
    skos:note "The capacity is conditional on a technique the essay does not describe, so no practice and no prerequisite with a prior step are entered."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ChaoismAndChaosMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Chaoism and Chaos Magic: A Personal View (electronic copy without imprint, a PDF of four leaves made on 2003-07-31 from a word-processor file; printed earlier in Chaos International no. 10, pp. 11-13, by a collection of excerpts dated 1993), leaf 4 of 4; read in the born-digital text layer of that PDF in the open scan archive item peter-j.-carroll-chaoism-and-chaos-magic" .

pmc:ChaosMagicChaoResearchConfirms a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The author's researches confirm that this is complete Chaos"@en, "Die Forschungen des Autors bestätigen, dass dies vollständiges Chaos ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author reports that his own researches confirm that the open-endedness of invocation and evocation is as chaotic as it sounds."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as an outcome report, apart from signs of success: no research is described."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ChaoismAndChaosMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Chaoism and Chaos Magic: A Personal View (electronic copy without imprint, a PDF of four leaves made on 2003-07-31 from a word-processor file; printed earlier in Chaos International no. 10, pp. 11-13, by a collection of excerpts dated 1993), leaf 4 of 4; read in the born-digital text layer of that PDF in the open scan archive item peter-j.-carroll-chaoism-and-chaos-magic" .

pmc:ChaosMagicChaoStrictTechniquesFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Without strict adherence to a handful of basic techniques there are no results"@en, "Ohne strikte Einhaltung weniger Grundtechniken keine Ergebnisse"@de ;
    skos:definition "Chaos Magic means for the author a few basic techniques that must be kept strictly to get results."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: results depend on strict adherence. It names a cause and no outcome anyone could notice, and the essay does not say which techniques are meant."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ChaoismAndChaosMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Chaoism and Chaos Magic: A Personal View (electronic copy without imprint, a PDF of four leaves made on 2003-07-31 from a word-processor file; printed earlier in Chaos International no. 10, pp. 11-13, by a collection of excerpts dated 1993), leaf 4 of 4; read in the born-digital text layer of that PDF in the open scan archive item peter-j.-carroll-chaoism-and-chaos-magic" .

pmc:ChaosMagicChaoFreedomBeyondTechnique a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Beyond its few strict techniques, a latitude of expression and aim unknown to earlier magic"@en, "Jenseits weniger strenger Techniken eine Freiheit des Ausdrucks und der Absicht, die frühere Magie nicht kannte"@de ;
    skos:definition "Beyond the basic techniques Chaos Magic is said to leave expression and intention freer than any earlier form of magic allowed."@en ;
    skos:note "A statement on how fixed the method is, paired with the node before it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ChaoismAndChaosMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Chaoism and Chaos Magic: A Personal View (electronic copy without imprint, a PDF of four leaves made on 2003-07-31 from a word-processor file; printed earlier in Chaos International no. 10, pp. 11-13, by a collection of excerpts dated 1993), leaf 4 of 4; read in the born-digital text layer of that PDF in the open scan archive item peter-j.-carroll-chaoism-and-chaos-magic" .
